  "note": "the sign is the finding, and it is the opposite of what this experiment was named for. A sales based backtest reports a larger error than the forecast makes against demand, not a smaller one, because the denominator shrinks faster than the numerator grows. So the bias does not flatter the forecast and a team reading it is not being told things are better than they are. They are being told the wrong forecaster is better, which is worse, because a pessimistic number invites no correction and a wrong ranking changes what gets shipped",
